[38;5;10m(int)[0m on an out-of-range double is UB in C. The reference build emits [38;5;10mcvttsd2si[0m, which returns [38;5;10mINT_MIN[0m. Rust's [38;5;10mas i32[0m saturates to [38;5;10mINT_MAX[0m instead, so [38;5;10mbad()[0m with empty input would have printed [38;5;10m2147483647[0m instead of [38;5;10m-2147483648[0m. I reproduced the x86-64 result explicitly. This is the bug the test case exists to demonstrate, so preserving it was the point.[0m[0m
