[38;5;10matof[0m needed a real [38;5;10mstrtod[0m. Rust's [38;5;10mf64[0m parser handles decimal forms with correct rounding, but glibc also accepts hex floats — [38;5;10m0x10[0m yields 16.0, printing [38;5;10m6[0m, where a naive parser stops at [38;5;10m0[0m and prints [38;5;10m-2147483648[0m. I wrote a hex path with round-to-nearest-even and a stepped [38;5;10mldexp[0m, plus C's [38;5;10minf[0m/[38;5;10mnan[0m/no-conversion rules and the longest-valid-prefix scan (so [38;5;10m7.5xyz[0m is 7.5 and [38;5;10m5e[0m is 5).[0m[0m
