[38;5;10mfgets[0m does not read across newlines, and leaves the remainder of an over-long line in the buffer. With a 20-byte buffer, a 30-digit first line means [38;5;10mgoodB2G[0m consumes 19 bytes and [38;5;10mbad()[0m picks up the tail — the second input line is never read. I implemented this over [38;5;10mStdinLock[0m's [38;5;10mfill_buf[0m/[38;5;10mconsume[0m so the buffer persists across both call sites, and treated the result as a C string (truncated at any embedded NUL) before parsing.[0m[0m
